.TH DQL-TARGET 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-target \- manage target adapters (fatboys, the per-engine co-processes)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql target list
.br
.B dql target install
.I PROFILE
.BI \-\-from " DIR"
.br
.B dql target verify
.SH DESCRIPTION
The slim
.B dql
binary speaks SQLite natively; other engines are reached through
separate adapter binaries named
.IR dql\-fatboy\-<profile> .
An adapter is resolved by searching, in order:
.IP 1. 3
.B DQL_FATBOY_DIR
(hard pin \(em when set, nothing else is searched);
.IP 2. 3
next to the
.B dql
binary;
.IP 3. 3
the adapter store
.RI ( ~/.local/share/delightql/fatboys/<version> );
.IP 4. 3
.BR PATH .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list ", " ls
Show each known adapter profile, whether it is installed, where it
resolves from, and its size. Also prints the adapter store path.
.TP
.BI install " PROFILE " \-\-from " DIR"
Copy the adapter binary for
.I PROFILE
(e.g.
.BR postgres ,
.BR duckdb )
from a local artifact directory into the adapter store.
.I DIR
holds either a bare
.I dql\-fatboy\-<profile>
or a release artifact named
.I dql\-fatboy\-<profile>\-<version>+<commit>\-<os>\-<arch>
(what scripts/release-build.py writes to dist/). The binary is verified
against the digests burned into this
.B dql
at release time \(em a mismatch refuses and nothing is installed.
Downloading from a published artifact host is a future source behind
the same verification; no host exists yet, so
.B \-\-from
is effectively required.
.TP
.B verify
Re-hash installed adapters against the digests burned into this
.B dql
at release time. Exits nonzero on any mismatch. Refuses on dev builds,
which carry no digests (see
.BR dql-version (1)).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on refusal (missing
.BR \-\-from ,
dev-build verify, digest mismatch).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DQL_FATBOY_DIR
Hard-pins adapter resolution to one directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ dql target list
$ dql target install postgres --from dist/
$ dql target verify
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-version (1),
.BR dql-server (1)
